Terminus, a bitmap font by Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov (https://terminus-font.sourceforge.net/),
under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. These are its 8x16 regular and bold
faces in PSF (version 1, 512 glyphs, with a Unicode table), as Debian's
console-setup ships them (console-setup-linux 1.237: Uni2-Terminus16.psf.gz,
Uni2-TerminusBold16.psf.gz, uncompressed):

  terminus16.psf        regular
  terminus16-bold.psf   bold

They cover Latin, Greek, Cyrillic and box drawing. MyNOS's display server
and its drawing primitives (module Gfx) read them from the system RAM disk
(doc/decisions/gui.md).
